From 7489e846e5513326b1f9a790480a7de6f42cce54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:20:37 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] Tabs: real instrument sounds and interactive notation help

- New SoundFont sample engine (data/soundfont): SF2 reader (memory-mapped),
  General MIDI sample synth (envelopes, mod env, LFOs, filter, exclusive
  classes, pitch bend, reverb, limiter), MIDI file reader, and a sampled
  score engine that plays guitar/bass StringScore events (bends, slides,
  hammer-ons, pull-offs, taps, vibrato, whammy, harmonics, palm mutes, dead
  notes, let ring) on recorded guitar/bass samples, one voice per string.
- GeneralUser GS 2.0.3 (32 MB) is downloaded once from this repo's release,
  SHA-256 verified, and loaded in the background. Synth then plays every part
  from samples; the MIDI player is muted and only keeps time. Falls back to
  the previous engines when not downloaded or switched off.
- Notation Help lists every mark for the part's instrument (39 guitar, 37
  bass, 31 kit pieces + drum techniques, 10 for other instruments), highlights
  the ones this song uses with the bar they first appear in, and plays a demo
  of any mark (or that bar of the song) on tap, through the same pipeline as
  playback.

